---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { companyName, supportEmail } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'June 7, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${companyName}`}
  description={`Privacy Policy for ${companyName} and the mobile applications I publish.`}
  path="/privacy"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-accent uppercase">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text sm:text-4xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-custom mt-12 space-y-10 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Who I am</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          {companyName} is a one-person iOS studio. I develop and publish mobile
          applications for iPhone and iPad. This Privacy Policy describes how I collect,
          use, and protect information when you use my apps or visit my website at
          pixelarclabs.com.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          If you have questions about this policy, contact me at{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
          >
            {supportEmail}
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Information I collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The information I collect depends on which {companyName} app you use and how
          you interact with it. In general, my apps may collect:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Account information</strong> — such as your email
            address or name, if you create an account or sign in.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">App data</strong> — information you enter or
            generate while using an app (for example, preferences, content, or records
            you create).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Device information</strong> — such as device model,
            operating system version, and app version, used to provide support and improve
            compatibility.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Usage information</strong> — such as feature usage
            and crash reports, to help me fix bugs and improve performance.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I do not sell your personal information. Specific apps may collect additional
          data as described in their in-app notices or settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">How I use your information</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">I use collected information to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>Provide, maintain, and improve my apps and services</li>
          <li>Authenticate your account and sync your data across devices</li>
          <li>Respond to support requests and communicate with you</li>
          <li>Diagnose technical issues and prevent fraud or abuse</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">How I store and protect data</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I take reasonable measures to protect your information using industry-standard
          security practices. Data may be stored on your device, or securely hosted on
          cloud infrastructure located in the United States.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I retain information only as long as needed to provide my services, comply
          with legal requirements, or resolve disputes. You can delete your account and
          associated data directly within the app's settings, or by contacting me at{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
          >
            {supportEmail}
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Some {companyName} apps may integrate with third-party services — such as cloud
          hosting, authentication, analytics, or payment providers — to deliver core
          functionality. These services process data according to their own privacy
          policies.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          For in-app purchases and subscriptions, payment processing is handled securely
          by Apple. I use third-party services to manage subscription access, but{' '}
          {companyName} does not collect, process, or store your raw payment details
          (like credit card numbers).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I choose providers carefully and limit the data shared to what is necessary for
          the service to function. Details about third-party integrations for a specific
          app may be available in that app's settings or documentation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Your rights and choices</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>Access the personal information I hold about you</li>
          <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
          <li>Object to or restrict certain processing</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          To exercise these rights, email me at{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
          >
            {supportEmail}
          </a>. I will respond within a reasonable timeframe.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          My apps are not directed at children under 13, and I do not knowingly collect
          personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided me with
          personal information, please contact me and I will delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When I do, I will revise
          the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of my apps after
          changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          {companyName}<br />
          Email:{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
          >
            {supportEmail}
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-16">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="text-sm text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-accent focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
      >
        &larr; Back to home
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
